    "viz_md_1": {
      "type": "splunk.markdown",
      "options": {
        "markdown": "### Basic paths, no splits\n\n**What this shows** - Every vehicle track from the lookup drawn as one path per vehicle, with the map auto-fitted to the data.\n\n**The SPL**\n\n```spl\n| inputlookup go_track_trackspoints.csv | lookup go_track_tracks.csv id as track_id | rex field=_time \"(?<date>^\\d+-\\d+-\\d+)\" | search $$date_filter_viz_1$$ $$track_id_viz_1$$ | eval id=track_id, speed=round(speed, 2), vehicle_type=if(car_or_bus == 1, \"car\", \"bus\"), description=\"<table align=\\\"center\\\" border=\\\"1\\\"><tr><th>id</th><th>time</th><th>vehicle type</th><th>speed</th></tr><tr><td align=\\\"center\\\">\".id.\"</td><td align=\\\"center\\\">\"._time.\"</td><td align=\\\"center\\\">\".vehicle_type.\"</td><td>\".speed.\"</td></tr></table>\", tooltip=description\n```\n\n**How it works**\n\n1. `inputlookup go_track_trackspoints.csv` loads the GPS points (`latitude`, `longitude`, `track_id`, `_time`); `lookup go_track_tracks.csv id as track_id` adds track details such as `speed` and `car_or_bus`.\n2. `rex` extracts the date from `_time`; `search $$date_filter_viz_1$$ $$track_id_viz_1$$` applies the two input filters.\n3. `eval` builds `id`, a rounded `speed`, `vehicle_type`, and the HTML `description` and `tooltip`.\n4. Maps+ receives one row per GPS point. `showPathLines=1` turns every row into a path vertex and `pathIdentifier=track_id` splits them into one path per vehicle.\n5. `pathSplits` is left at 0, so `pathSplitInterval=30` has no effect here.\n\n**Field formats and rules**\n\n| Field | Expected format | Rule / gotcha |\n|---|---|---|\n| `latitude` | decimal degrees (number) | Exact lowercase name. Here it comes straight from the lookup. Every row is a path vertex, so every row needs coordinates. |\n| `longitude` | decimal degrees (number) | Exact lowercase name. |\n| `_time` | timestamp Maps+ can parse | Used by `pathSplits` and playback. Maps+ never sorts: rows are drawn in result order, and this query relies on the lookup's row order. |\n| `track_id` | any text; the field named in `pathIdentifier` | Splits rows into paths. Without `pathIdentifier`, all rows form one path. |\n| `description` | HTML text | Click popup; a path takes it from its first row. Escape any event text you put in it. |\n| `tooltip` | HTML text | Hover tooltip; a path takes it from its first row. |\n| `id, speed, vehicle_type` | any | Not reserved Maps+ fields: not drawn, but passed to drilldown. |\n\n**Try it**\n\n- Add `| sort 0 _time` before `eval` to guarantee time order, whatever the lookup order.\n- Edit `pathColorList` in the Format panel to recolour the paths.\n\n> **Studio note:** Studio multiselect inputs ignore the classic prefix (`track_id=`), `valuePrefix`/`valueSuffix` and `delimiter`; values are comma-joined with no wrapping, so the token no longer expands to `track_id=\"16\" OR track_id=\"17\"`. Only the **All** choice (`*`) gives a valid filter, so the inputs default to All. The query text is unchanged. Tokens in the SPL above may show their current values when Studio renders this panel.\n\n**Basemap:** this example uses keyless OpenFreeMap vector tiles (`useOpenFreeMap` = 1). CARTO basemaps need a free API key: see **Help > Basemaps & API keys** for how to get one and where to put it (**Map Tile Override**)."
      }
    },
    "viz_md_2": {
      "type": "splunk.markdown",
      "options": {
        "markdown": "### Paths split on time gaps\n\n**What this shows** - The same tracks, but a path is broken wherever consecutive points are more than 10 seconds apart.\n\n**The SPL**\n\n```spl\n| inputlookup go_track_trackspoints.csv | lookup go_track_tracks.csv id as track_id | rex field=_time \"(?<date>^\\d+-\\d+-\\d+)\" | search $$date_filter_viz_2$$ $$track_id_viz_2$$ | eval id=track_id, speed=round(speed, 2), vehicle_type=if(car_or_bus == 1, \"car\", \"bus\"), description=\"<table align=\\\"center\\\" border=\\\"1\\\"><tr><th>id</th><th>time</th><th>vehicle type</th><th>speed</th></tr><tr><td align=\\\"center\\\">\".id.\"</td><td align=\\\"center\\\">\"._time.\"</td><td align=\\\"center\\\">\".vehicle_type.\"</td><td>\".speed.\"</td></tr></table>\", tooltip=description\n```\n\n**How it works**\n\n1. `inputlookup go_track_trackspoints.csv` loads the GPS points (`latitude`, `longitude`, `track_id`, `_time`); `lookup go_track_tracks.csv id as track_id` adds track details such as `speed` and `car_or_bus`.\n2. `rex` extracts the date from `_time`; `search $$date_filter_viz_2$$ $$track_id_viz_2$$` applies the two input filters.\n3. `eval` builds `id`, a rounded `speed`, `vehicle_type`, and the HTML `description` and `tooltip`.\n4. Maps+ receives one row per GPS point. `showPathLines=1` turns every row into a path vertex and `pathIdentifier=track_id` splits them into one path per vehicle.\n5. `pathSplits=1` breaks a path when the gap between rows exceeds `pathSplitInterval`; here `pathSplitInterval=10` (seconds). `_time` drives the gap test, so the rows must be in time order.\n\n**Field formats and rules**\n\n| Field | Expected format | Rule / gotcha |\n|---|---|---|\n| `latitude` | decimal degrees (number) | Exact lowercase name. Here it comes straight from the lookup. Every row is a path vertex, so every row needs coordinates. |\n| `longitude` | decimal degrees (number) | Exact lowercase name. |\n| `_time` | timestamp Maps+ can parse | Used by `pathSplits` and playback. Maps+ never sorts: rows are drawn in result order, and this query relies on the lookup's row order. |\n| `track_id` | any text; the field named in `pathIdentifier` | Splits rows into paths. Without `pathIdentifier`, all rows form one path. |\n| `description` | HTML text | Click popup; a path takes it from its first row. Escape any event text you put in it. |\n| `tooltip` | HTML text | Hover tooltip; a path takes it from its first row. |\n| `id, speed, vehicle_type` | any | Not reserved Maps+ fields: not drawn, but passed to drilldown. |\n\n**Try it**\n\n- Raise `pathSplitInterval` to 60 and the short gaps stop splitting the paths.\n- Set `pathSplits=0` to compare with the previous map.\n\n> **Studio note:** Studio multiselect inputs ignore the classic prefix (`track_id=`), `valuePrefix`/`valueSuffix` and `delimiter`; values are comma-joined with no wrapping, so the token no longer expands to `track_id=\"16\" OR track_id=\"17\"`. Only the **All** choice (`*`) gives a valid filter, so the inputs default to All. The query text is unchanged. The date input keeps its classic default `2014-09-17`, which Studio inserts as a bare value rather than `date=\"2014-09-17\"`.\n\n**Basemap:** this example uses keyless OpenFreeMap vector tiles (`useOpenFreeMap` = 1). CARTO basemaps need a free API key: see **Help > Basemaps & API keys** for how to get one and where to put it (**Map Tile Override**)."
      }
    },
    "viz_md_3": {
      "type": "splunk.markdown",
      "options": {
        "markdown": "### Styled paths and layers\n\n**What this shows** - Vehicles 16, 17, 20, 22 and 23 drawn as styled paths grouped into two layers; markers are hidden so only the paths show.\n\n**The SPL**\n\n```spl\n| inputlookup go_track_trackspoints.csv | lookup go_track_tracks.csv id as track_id | rex field=_time \"(?<date>^\\d+-\\d+-\\d+)\" | search $$date_filter_viz_3$$ $$track_id_viz_3$$ | eval markerVisibility=\"hidden\", id=track_id, speed=round(speed, 2), vehicle_type=if(car_or_bus == 1, \"car\", \"bus\"), description=\"car \".id, tooltip=description, pathColor=case(like(id, \"16\"), \"#e50de5\"), pathWeight=case(like(id, \"16\"), \"20\"), pathOpacity=case(like(id, \"16\"), \"1.0\"), antPath=\"true\", layerDescription=case(like(pathLayer, \"cars-16-20\"), \"cars-16-20\", like(pathLayer, \"cars-17-22-23\"), \"cars-17-22-23\"), pathLayer=case(like(id, \"16\"), \"cars-16-20\", like(id, \"17\"), \"cars-17-22-23\", like(id, \"20\"), \"cars-16-20\", like(id, \"22\"), \"cars-17-22-23\", like(id, \"23\"), \"cars-17-22-23\"), layerPriority=case(like(pathLayer, \"cars-16-20\"), 10, like(pathLayer, \"cars-17-22-23\"), 5)\n```\n\n**How it works**\n\n1. `inputlookup go_track_trackspoints.csv` loads the GPS points (`latitude`, `longitude`, `track_id`, `_time`); `lookup go_track_tracks.csv id as track_id` adds track details such as `speed` and `car_or_bus`.\n2. `rex` extracts the date from `_time`; `search $$date_filter_viz_3$$ $$track_id_viz_3$$` applies the two input filters.\n3. `eval` sets `markerVisibility=\"hidden\"`, and uses `case(like(id, ...))` to give vehicle 16 `pathColor`, `pathWeight` and `pathOpacity`, and to put vehicles into `pathLayer` groups with a `layerPriority`.\n4. Maps+ takes a path's style from its first row, so `case()` only needs to match the ids you want styled.\n5. Gotcha: `eval` runs left to right, and `layerDescription` tests `pathLayer` before `pathLayer` is assigned. As written, `layerDescription` can only match a `pathLayer` already in the lookup.\n\n**Field formats and rules**\n\n| Field | Expected format | Rule / gotcha |\n|---|---|---|\n| `latitude` | decimal degrees (number) | Exact lowercase name. Here it comes straight from the lookup. Every row is a path vertex, so every row needs coordinates. |\n| `longitude` | decimal degrees (number) | Exact lowercase name. |\n| `_time` | timestamp Maps+ can parse | Used by `pathSplits` and playback. Maps+ never sorts: rows are drawn in result order, and this query relies on the lookup's row order. |\n| `track_id` | any text; the field named in `pathIdentifier` | Splits rows into paths. Without `pathIdentifier`, all rows form one path. |\n| `description` | HTML text | Click popup; a path takes it from its first row. Escape any event text you put in it. |\n| `tooltip` | HTML text | Hover tooltip; a path takes it from its first row. |\n| `markerVisibility` | `\"true\"` / `\"marker\"` shows; anything else hides | Every row also draws a marker; this hides them so only the path shows. The documented off value is `\"false\"`. |\n| `pathColor` | CSS colour | Set for vehicle 16 only; the others fall back to `pathColorList`. |\n| `pathWeight` | integer, default 5 | Line width in pixels. |\n| `pathOpacity` | 0 to 1, default 0.5 | Line opacity. |\n| `pathLayer` | text | Layer-control entry for the path (default: the path id). |\n| `layerDescription` | HTML text | Label in the layer control; for path layers the first row wins. |\n| `layerPriority` | integer | Pane order of the layer. |\n\n**Try it**\n\n- Move the `layerDescription=case(...)` expression after `pathLayer=case(...)` to see layer labels in the layer control.\n- Change `pathWeight` for id 16 from `\"20\"` to `\"8\"` for a thinner line.\n\n> **Studio note:** Studio multiselect inputs ignore the classic prefix (`track_id=`), `valuePrefix`/`valueSuffix` and `delimiter`; values are comma-joined with no wrapping, so the token no longer expands to `track_id=\"16\" OR track_id=\"17\"`. Only the **All** choice (`*`) gives a valid filter, so the inputs default to All. The query text is unchanged. On Maps+ 4.6.9 and earlier, a Studio cell that is null counts as set (the `case()` fields below are null for non-matching rows); fixed in the unreleased 4.6.10.\n\n**Basemap:** this example uses keyless OpenFreeMap vector tiles (`useOpenFreeMap` = 1). CARTO basemaps need a free API key: see **Help > Basemaps & API keys** for how to get one and where to put it (**Map Tile Override**)."
      }
    }
